            <ArticleTitle>Primary Colonic Lymphoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s11605-017-3472-4</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Primary colonic lymphoma is a rare large bowel malignancy usually found in the cecum or rectosigmoid junction. Because of its non-specific symptoms, patients often present with advanced disease requiring surgical intervention. Nevertheless, resection followed by chemotherapy appears to offer the best prognosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
